# Techniche App-Backend API Documentation

This document outlines the REST API endpoints provided by the `app-backend` microservice specifically built for the Flutter mobile application. 

**Base URL**: `http://<SERVER_IP>:3002/api`

---

## 1. Authentication

### Google Login
**Endpoint:** `POST /auth/google-login`  
**Description:** Authenticates a user using their Google ID. If the user doesn't exist, an account is created automatically.
**Auth Required:** No

**Request Body (JSON):**
```json
{
  "email": "student@iitg.ac.in", // Required
  "googleId": "1234567890",      // Required
  "name": "John Doe"             // Optional
}
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "message": "Login successful",
  "token": "eyJhbGciOi...", 
  "user": {
    "id": 1,
    "email": "student@iitg.ac.in",
    "googleId": "1234567890",
    "authProvider": "google",
    "fcmToken": "device_token_abc"
  }
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> Save the `token` string securely on the device. All subsequent requests require this token to be sent in the request headers as either `Authorization: Bearer <token>` or `token: <token>`.

### Save FCM Token
**Endpoint:** `POST /auth/fcm-token`  
**Description:** Saves the Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) token for push notifications. The app should call this after the user has successfully logged in and granted notification permissions.
**Auth Required:** Yes

**Request Body (JSON):**
```json
{
  "fcmToken": "device_token_abc"
}
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "message": "FCM token saved successfully."
}
```

